1
00:01:29,000 --> 00:01:32,000
 Ninja vs. Indy Ryozu

2
00:01:35,000 --> 00:01:36,000
 Good morning.

3
00:01:36,000 --> 00:01:37,000
 Good morning.

4
00:01:37,000 --> 00:01:39,000
 Good morning.

5
00:01:40,000 --> 00:01:43,000
 Ryozu, what's with that outfit?

6
00:01:44,000 --> 00:01:48,000
 Oh, I was just about to go on patrol.

7
00:01:48,000 --> 00:01:51,000
 When did you become a mountain patrol?

8
00:01:51,000 --> 00:01:53,000
 Well, I've been armed lately.

9
00:01:53,000 --> 00:01:57,000
I can't be a patrol without
this kind of equipment.

10
00:01:57,000 --> 00:01:58,597
 Don't lie!

11
00:01:58,800 --> 00:02:02,000
No matter how much I
ask, you don't tell me.

12
00:02:03,000 --> 00:02:05,000
 Ryozu, are you ready?

13
00:02:05,000 --> 00:02:07,000
 It's about time to go.

14
00:02:07,000 --> 00:02:09,000
 Hey, are you going to the station?

15
00:02:09,000 --> 00:02:11,000
 Go straight here.

16
00:02:11,000 --> 00:02:12,000
 I'm sorry.

17
00:02:12,000 --> 00:02:13,000
 Please go ahead.

18
00:02:13,000 --> 00:02:14,000
 I'll be right there.

19
00:02:14,000 --> 00:02:17,000
 Ryozu, what do you mean?

20
00:02:17,000 --> 00:02:18,000
 Huh?

21
00:02:18,000 --> 00:02:21,000
 Isn't that Himeji Shuzaburo?

22
00:02:21,000 --> 00:02:24,552
Is Himeji Shuzaburo that
famous archaeologist?

23
00:02:24,739 --> 00:02:28,000
Last year, he tried to dig
up Akagi-san with a bulldozer

24
00:02:28,000 --> 00:02:31,000
 to discover Tokugawa's buried gold.

25
00:02:31,000 --> 00:02:33,000
 In the end, it was a failure.

26
00:02:33,000 --> 00:02:37,000
Well, it's about
time to go on patrol.

27
00:02:37,000 --> 00:02:42,000
Ryo-chan, don't tell me you're going to
look for the buried gold with that person.

28
00:02:42,000 --> 00:02:44,000
 Buried gold?

29
00:02:44,000 --> 00:02:47,000
Are you planning
something that's not good?

30
00:02:47,000 --> 00:02:50,000
It's rude to say
something that's not good.

31
00:02:50,000 --> 00:02:52,000
 I want you to say it's a man's dream.

32
00:02:52,000 --> 00:02:53,000
 A man's dream.

33
00:02:53,000 --> 00:02:56,000
 What's a man's dream?

34
00:02:56,000 --> 00:03:00,000
 It's best to work hard and live hard.

35
00:03:00,000 --> 00:03:05,000
It's not a man's job
to look for buried gold.

36
00:03:05,000 --> 00:03:10,000
Senpai, it's not that
easy to find buried gold.

37
00:03:10,000 --> 00:03:12,000
 Well, it's up to you.

38
00:03:12,000 --> 00:03:13,000
 Alright, guys.

39
00:03:13,000 --> 00:03:15,000
 See you tomorrow.

40
00:03:15,000 --> 00:03:16,000
 Wait!

41
00:03:16,000 --> 00:03:18,000
 Wait, Ryozu!

42
00:03:18,000 --> 00:03:23,000
 That man has everything to do with money.

43
00:03:25,000 --> 00:03:27,000
 But is it really true?

44
00:03:27,000 --> 00:03:30,000
It's a castle that hasn't been
discovered by anyone yet.

45
00:03:30,000 --> 00:03:33,000
 You'll have to believe me.

46
00:03:33,000 --> 00:03:34,000
 Hello.

47
00:03:34,000 --> 00:03:36,000
 Hello.

48
00:03:36,000 --> 00:03:38,000
 Hello, hello.

49
00:03:38,000 --> 00:03:39,000
 Look.

50
00:03:39,000 --> 00:03:41,000
 There are so many men.

51
00:03:41,000 --> 00:03:43,000
 That's why it's called Magoroshi Castle.

52
00:03:43,000 --> 00:03:46,000
 There's a castle in the middle of the sea.

53
00:03:46,000 --> 00:03:48,000
 It's called Magoroshi Castle.

54
00:03:48,000 --> 00:03:50,000
 In the name of that castle,

55
00:03:50,000 --> 00:03:53,000
 it's the best place to find gold.

56
00:03:53,000 --> 00:03:56,000
 There's no gold in the real place,

57
00:03:56,000 --> 00:04:01,000
but the castle used to
be an imaginary monster.

58
00:04:01,000 --> 00:04:05,000
If you put it on the building,
it'll protect you from fires.

59
00:04:05,000 --> 00:04:07,000
 It doesn't matter if it's a shit,

60
00:04:07,000 --> 00:04:11,000
but that castle is
made of real gold, right?

61
00:04:11,000 --> 00:04:12,000
 Yes.

62
00:04:12,000 --> 00:04:14,000
 There was a gold mountain in the sea,

63
00:04:14,000 --> 00:04:17,000
 so they melted a lot of gold and made it.

64
00:04:17,000 --> 00:04:20,000
 I'm not really interested in gold,

65
00:04:20,000 --> 00:04:24,000
 but it's worth 100 million yen.

66
00:04:24,000 --> 00:04:26,000
 What? 100 million yen?

67
00:04:26,000 --> 00:04:28,000
 Tell me that first.

68
00:04:28,000 --> 00:04:31,000
 If you know that, I won't be here.

69
00:04:31,000 --> 00:04:32,661
 Hurry up and find the castle.

70
00:04:33,483 --> 00:04:37,483
I just want to discover the
hidden castle of Takeda Shigen.

71
00:04:41,000 --> 00:04:43,445
 There's no way out.

72
00:04:43,664 --> 00:04:44,664
 Which way?

73
00:04:44,694 --> 00:04:46,054
This way.

74
00:04:49,804 --> 00:04:52,000
 I wonder if this is the right way.

75
00:04:52,000 --> 00:04:53,093
 There's no mistake.

76
00:04:53,444 --> 00:04:54,608
Yes.
It's the right way.

77
00:04:57,414 --> 00:04:59,414
 What is this?

78
00:05:03,000 --> 00:05:05,131
This looks like the
hidden castle of Shigen.

79
00:05:05,156 --> 00:05:06,156
 Hey, hey!

80
00:05:06,181 --> 00:05:09,181
 We're not looking for a place to hide.

81
00:05:13,000 --> 00:05:17,000
 You're not talking about that, are you?

82
00:05:17,000 --> 00:05:19,000
 No, no.

83
00:05:19,000 --> 00:05:20,000
 That's strange.

84
00:05:20,000 --> 00:05:23,000
 There's no place like this on the map.

85
00:05:23,000 --> 00:05:24,000
 Oh, no.

86
00:05:24,000 --> 00:05:26,355
 We're going to lose.

87
00:05:26,380 --> 00:05:28,000
 Oh, look.

88
00:05:28,000 --> 00:05:30,000
 There's a path.

89
00:05:30,000 --> 00:05:33,000
 There's no mistake in the hidden castle.

90
00:05:38,000 --> 00:05:40,000
 It's a dead end.

91
00:05:40,000 --> 00:05:43,000
 It's a really good hidden castle.

92
00:05:45,319 --> 00:05:49,126
 Maybe it's like this.

93
00:05:49,345 --> 00:05:51,383
 Hey, let me out.

94
00:05:51,408 --> 00:05:53,000
 What are you doing?

95
00:05:53,000 --> 00:05:56,724
 This is valuable information that I found.

96
00:05:56,749 --> 00:05:58,000
 Give it to me.

97
00:05:58,000 --> 00:05:59,000
 No.

98
00:05:59,000 --> 00:06:00,000
 Give it to me.

99
00:06:00,000 --> 00:06:01,000
 No.

100
00:06:15,000 --> 00:06:17,000
 Are you okay?

101
00:06:17,000 --> 00:06:19,586
 It seems to be safe.

102
00:06:19,611 --> 00:06:23,000
 But it seems to have rolled down a lot.

103
00:06:25,000 --> 00:06:27,690
 Thanks to you, it's a lot shorter.

104
00:06:27,715 --> 00:06:29,200
 Don't mess with me.

105
00:06:29,590 --> 00:06:32,208
 Oh, there's a house there.

106
00:06:32,794 --> 00:06:34,567
 It looks like a tea shop.

107
00:06:35,000 --> 00:06:38,000
 Hey, let me take a break.

108
00:06:41,000 --> 00:06:44,000
 Welcome.

109
00:06:44,000 --> 00:06:46,000
 I'll have tea and dango.

110
00:06:48,585 --> 00:06:51,740
Where are you two going?

111
00:06:51,765 --> 00:06:55,382
Actually, there's something
we're looking for around here.

112
00:06:57,000 --> 00:06:59,000
 Something to look for?

113
00:06:59,000 --> 00:07:01,367
 What kind of thing is that?

114
00:07:01,392 --> 00:07:06,000
No, no. I was just walking down
the mountain and lost my way.

115
00:07:06,000 --> 00:07:07,000
 Right?

116
00:07:07,000 --> 00:07:08,000
 Yes, yes, yes.

117
00:07:08,000 --> 00:07:11,000
 But what is it?

118
00:07:12,000 --> 00:07:16,000
No one will come even if they
put a tea shop in such a place.

119
00:07:16,000 --> 00:07:17,000
 What?

120
00:07:17,000 --> 00:07:21,000
Sometimes there are people
who come to the road like you.

121
00:07:21,000 --> 00:07:23,000
 Don't worry.

122
00:07:23,000 --> 00:07:24,000
 Oh, I see.

123
00:07:28,000 --> 00:07:31,000
Now, if you eat dango,
you can go down here.

124
00:07:31,000 --> 00:07:34,000
If you go for a while,
you'll hit the mountain road.

125
00:07:37,000 --> 00:07:39,000
 What should I do, Mr. Ryo?

126
00:07:39,000 --> 00:07:42,274
 I think it's definitely ahead of here.

127
00:07:42,299 --> 00:07:45,139
 There's a smell of gold ahead of here.

128
00:07:45,164 --> 00:07:48,000
I'm sorry.
I just put out a fire.

129
00:07:50,000 --> 00:07:53,000
 Grandpa, I'll put the tea here.

130
00:07:53,000 --> 00:07:55,000
 I don't need to fish.

131
00:07:55,000 --> 00:07:56,000
 Wait a minute.

132
00:07:58,000 --> 00:08:01,000
What are you going to
do with this 1,000 yen?

133
00:08:01,000 --> 00:08:03,000
 What? Is it too much?

134
00:08:04,000 --> 00:08:06,000
 Don't talk nonsense.

135
00:08:06,000 --> 00:08:08,000
 One cup of tea is 500 yen.

136
00:08:08,000 --> 00:08:10,000
 Three dango is 1,000 yen.

137
00:08:10,000 --> 00:08:12,000
 Two people together is 3,000 yen.

138
00:08:12,000 --> 00:08:14,000
 You need to pay me well.

139
00:08:14,000 --> 00:08:16,000
 3,000 yen?

140
00:08:16,000 --> 00:08:18,000
 Damn it.

141
00:08:18,000 --> 00:08:21,000
Why are you looking
at the customer's foot?

142
00:08:21,000 --> 00:08:25,000
The electricity, gas, and water
don't pass through this mountain.

143
00:08:25,000 --> 00:08:27,000
 Even if it's 3,000 yen, it's not worth it.

144
00:08:27,000 --> 00:08:29,000
I understand. I understand.
I'll pay. I'll pay.

145
00:08:29,000 --> 00:08:31,000
 Anyway, let's hurry up.

146
00:08:35,000 --> 00:08:37,000
 Thank you very much.

147
00:08:37,000 --> 00:08:39,000
 Come again.

148
00:08:39,000 --> 00:08:41,000
 Don't come again.

149
00:08:41,000 --> 00:08:42,000
 No, no.

150
00:08:42,000 --> 00:08:44,000
 You can't go there.

151
00:08:44,000 --> 00:08:46,000
I told you that the
mountain road is over there.

152
00:08:46,000 --> 00:08:48,000
 It's a snowstorm ahead of here.

153
00:08:48,000 --> 00:08:50,000
If you enter without
permission, you will be beaten.

154
00:08:50,000 --> 00:08:52,000
 Beaten?

155
00:08:52,000 --> 00:08:53,000
 Idiot.

156
00:08:53,000 --> 00:08:55,000
 Get out of here.

157
00:09:05,000 --> 00:09:08,000
 It was really a snowstorm.

158
00:09:08,000 --> 00:09:09,000
 Damn it.

159
00:09:09,000 --> 00:09:12,000
 It's the same as the old man said.

160
00:09:12,000 --> 00:09:16,525
 I'm sure there's a ghost town near here.

161
00:09:18,000 --> 00:09:21,586
 I can't climb this rock wall.

162
00:09:21,726 --> 00:09:24,000
 I'm going to take a shower now.

163
00:09:25,000 --> 00:09:28,000
It's frustrating, but I
have to get it back.

164
00:09:32,485 --> 00:09:33,485
 What's wrong?

165
00:09:33,510 --> 00:09:35,000
 Come with me.

166
00:09:35,000 --> 00:09:37,580
 Can't you take a shower alone?

167
00:09:38,000 --> 00:09:39,000
 I can.

168
00:09:39,000 --> 00:09:41,000
 No, I can't.

169
00:09:41,000 --> 00:09:43,000
 Pour some water here.

170
00:09:43,000 --> 00:09:45,000
 Put some sand on it.

171
00:09:45,000 --> 00:09:47,000
 I'm not a cat.

172
00:09:47,000 --> 00:09:49,000
 Like this?

173
00:09:55,000 --> 00:09:58,000
 You can hear the water flowing.

174
00:09:58,000 --> 00:10:01,000
 There seems to be something down there.

175
00:10:01,000 --> 00:10:04,000
 But I can't move this big thing.

176
00:10:04,000 --> 00:10:05,000
 It moved.

177
00:10:05,000 --> 00:10:06,000
 What's this?

178
00:10:06,000 --> 00:10:07,000
 Is it a limestone?

179
00:10:07,000 --> 00:10:10,000
 Mr. Ryo, there must be something.

180
00:10:19,396 --> 00:10:20,396
 Look.

181
00:10:20,421 --> 00:10:21,981
 It's the light of the exit.

182
00:10:28,000 --> 00:10:30,000
 It's white.

183
00:10:30,000 --> 00:10:33,000
 It's a ghost town.

184
00:10:35,491 --> 00:10:36,724
 I did it.

185
00:10:36,749 --> 00:10:38,616
 It's a golden limestone.

186
00:10:39,889 --> 00:10:43,000
I found it.
I finally found it.

187
00:10:43,000 --> 00:10:48,000
Normally, a castle is built
to look down on the world.

188
00:10:48,000 --> 00:10:51,000
 It's like a ghost town.

189
00:10:51,000 --> 00:10:53,000
 That's why it's a ghost town.

190
00:10:53,000 --> 00:10:57,000
The lord, who was the
descendant of the new emperor,

191
00:10:57,000 --> 00:11:00,274
 built a castle in this secluded castle.

192
00:11:00,852 --> 00:11:05,367
I can agree that I
couldn't find it until now.

193
00:11:07,342 --> 00:11:10,000
 But how do you get that?

194
00:11:10,000 --> 00:11:13,000
 There are no bridges around here.

195
00:11:13,000 --> 00:11:18,000
This means that you have to
use bridges and bridges to get in.

196
00:11:18,000 --> 00:11:20,000
 Bridges and bridges?

197
00:11:21,898 --> 00:11:23,898
 Could it be that?

198
00:11:26,000 --> 00:11:28,000
 What? I can't reach it.

199
00:11:29,000 --> 00:11:31,000
 How about using another one?

200
00:11:31,000 --> 00:11:33,000
 It's the same length.

201
00:11:33,000 --> 00:11:36,000
It's the same thing if
you use another one.

202
00:11:37,000 --> 00:11:38,000
 Wait.

203
00:11:38,000 --> 00:11:41,000
 Use bridges and bridges.

204
00:11:41,000 --> 00:11:42,000
 I got it.

205
00:11:42,000 --> 00:11:45,000
 This way, I can cross it.

206
00:11:45,000 --> 00:11:46,000
 I see.

207
00:11:46,000 --> 00:11:50,000
So you use the bridge of
wood and the bridge of ice.

208
00:11:54,647 --> 00:11:57,647
 Open this gate.

209
00:12:07,118 --> 00:12:09,346
 Damn it. I can't open it.

210
00:12:09,430 --> 00:12:11,430
 It was a hole.

211
00:12:12,454 --> 00:12:14,486
 What a meaningless sign.

212
00:12:15,201 --> 00:12:18,201
 Now it's a big iron gate.

213
00:12:21,000 --> 00:12:24,000
I won't be surprised no
matter how hard I push it.

214
00:12:24,000 --> 00:12:28,000
When Tatsumi meets a
horse, it becomes a gate.

215
00:12:28,000 --> 00:12:29,000
 A code?

216
00:12:29,000 --> 00:12:32,000
 Then this elephant is probably the hint.

217
00:12:32,000 --> 00:12:34,000
 But it's strange. There's no horse.

218
00:12:34,000 --> 00:12:37,000
 Isn't horse a direction?

219
00:12:37,000 --> 00:12:41,000
 In the Edo period, horse is a word that indicates the direction of the south.

220
00:12:41,000 --> 00:12:42,000
 That's it.

221
00:12:42,000 --> 00:12:45,000
 The elephant of Tatsumi goes south.

222
00:12:45,000 --> 00:12:47,000
 What is Tatsumi?

223
00:12:48,000 --> 00:12:51,000
 Tatsumi means the elephant of Edo and the snake.

224
00:12:51,000 --> 00:12:52,000
 Okay.

225
00:12:52,000 --> 00:12:54,000
 The elephant and the snake go south.

226
00:12:54,000 --> 00:12:56,000
 Which one goes south?

227
00:12:57,000 --> 00:13:00,000
 I can't reach the radio wave.

228
00:13:00,476 --> 00:13:02,476
 Okay. Let's go with that hand.

229
00:13:03,696 --> 00:13:05,000
 What do you do when you cut the wood?

230
00:13:05,000 --> 00:13:07,000
 Look at the cut.

231
00:13:07,000 --> 00:13:10,000
 The one that's grown bigger in the forest is south.

232
00:13:10,000 --> 00:13:11,000
 That way.

233
00:13:11,000 --> 00:13:13,000
 Look at the elephant.

234
00:13:14,000 --> 00:13:15,408
 And the snake.

235
00:13:15,678 --> 00:13:16,678
 That's not a snake.

236
00:13:16,703 --> 00:13:18,703
 It's the soil.

237
00:13:24,000 --> 00:13:26,950
 You made a bad elephant.

238
00:13:26,975 --> 00:13:29,975
 I have to be more careful.

239
00:13:30,000 --> 00:13:33,435
Anyway, the gate is open,
so there's no problem.

240
00:13:41,000 --> 00:13:44,000
 That man has finally come this far.

241
00:13:45,007 --> 00:13:48,268
 It's finally my turn.

242
00:13:48,519 --> 00:13:55,000
For 400 years, we have
been protecting this castle.

243
00:13:56,703 --> 00:13:57,703
 Shingen Kou.

244
00:13:57,784 --> 00:14:04,068
 Now I'm alone, but I'm still young.

245
00:14:04,093 --> 00:14:07,260
 Let's show them what we've got.

246
00:14:31,000 --> 00:14:34,000
This looks like a ghost house.

247
00:14:34,000 --> 00:14:37,000
It's been hundreds of
years since it was built.

248
00:14:37,000 --> 00:14:41,000
Well, I don't have any
complaints about it.

249
00:14:41,000 --> 00:14:44,000
 Anyway, we have to climb to the top.

250
00:14:45,000 --> 00:14:47,000
 If we go that way...

251
00:14:50,000 --> 00:14:53,490
There's a fishing trap,
so we have to be careful.

252
00:14:53,515 --> 00:14:55,515
 Then tell me quickly.

253
00:14:57,000 --> 00:14:59,000
 I'm still alive.

254
00:15:00,000 --> 00:15:02,000
 I don't know what kind of trap there is.

255
00:15:03,000 --> 00:15:04,000
 Okay, let's go upstairs.

256
00:15:09,000 --> 00:15:11,000
 It's like a staircase.

257
00:15:12,000 --> 00:15:14,000
 I can't go on like this.

258
00:15:15,648 --> 00:15:17,648
They are in trouble,
They are in trouble.

259
00:15:23,000 --> 00:15:25,000
 Hey, come up here.

260
00:15:26,000 --> 00:15:28,000
 There is still a trap.

261
00:15:34,000 --> 00:15:35,000
 What?

262
00:15:38,000 --> 00:15:39,000
 Wait a minute.

263
00:15:43,000 --> 00:15:44,000
 How about this?

264
00:15:54,989 --> 00:15:57,989
 The trap is getting more and more serious.

265
00:15:58,014 --> 00:16:02,412
 I have to find about 10 gold coins.

266
00:16:02,437 --> 00:16:04,437
 I have a lot of money.

267
00:16:05,375 --> 00:16:07,465
 Then I'll use the next trick.

268
00:16:10,000 --> 00:16:12,000
 It's the third floor.

269
00:16:12,000 --> 00:16:15,000
The top floor is the fifth
floor, so it's still half way.

270
00:16:16,000 --> 00:16:18,000
 Anyway, I'm going to look for the stairs.

271
00:16:20,000 --> 00:16:22,000
 What's that?

272
00:16:22,000 --> 00:16:24,000
 There's something written inside.

273
00:16:24,000 --> 00:16:26,000
 The top floor of Tenshukaku.

274
00:16:27,000 --> 00:16:30,000
 Isn't this an elevator?

275
00:16:31,000 --> 00:16:33,000
 Hey, isn't that another trick?

276
00:16:34,000 --> 00:16:36,000
 Oh, there's an old gold box here.

277
00:16:36,000 --> 00:16:37,000
 What?

278
00:16:38,000 --> 00:16:40,444
 I thought it was just a brass plate.

279
00:16:42,484 --> 00:16:43,484
 What?

280
00:16:48,000 --> 00:16:49,432
 I can't open it.

281
00:16:50,461 --> 00:16:51,461
 Who is it?

282
00:16:52,234 --> 00:16:56,234
I thought it was a
bone, but it's still blue.

283
00:16:59,000 --> 00:17:02,000
 You're the old man in the tea shop.

284
00:17:02,000 --> 00:17:04,000
 Who is the old man in the tea shop?

285
00:17:04,000 --> 00:17:07,000
 I'm not a greedy fool.

286
00:17:07,000 --> 00:17:09,543
 Get out of here.

287
00:17:09,568 --> 00:17:16,369
I can't let you get out of this castle,
which is protected by the Maboroshi clan.

288
00:17:17,195 --> 00:17:18,463
 Maboroshi clan?

289
00:17:18,601 --> 00:17:20,601
 It's Maboroshi.

290
00:17:21,000 --> 00:17:24,000
Your goal is to be the
president of the gold.

291
00:17:24,000 --> 00:17:26,000
 But you can't touch it with one finger

292
00:17:26,025 --> 00:17:28,631
 as long as I'm here.

293
00:17:29,000 --> 00:17:30,000
 Is that so?

294
00:17:30,000 --> 00:17:33,000
 I can't even touch it with one finger.

295
00:17:33,000 --> 00:17:35,000
 That's not a big deal.

296
00:17:35,000 --> 00:17:37,000
 If you can touch it,

297
00:17:37,000 --> 00:17:40,000
 I'll give you the president of the gold.

298
00:17:40,000 --> 00:17:43,000
 But you can't get out of there.

299
00:17:45,744 --> 00:17:46,744
 Damn it.

300
00:17:46,769 --> 00:17:49,000
 Don't forget what you just said.

301
00:17:49,000 --> 00:17:51,000
 I'll give you 10 billion yen.

302
00:17:54,000 --> 00:17:55,000
 What a guy.

303
00:17:57,000 --> 00:17:58,000
 That's it.

304
00:17:59,796 --> 00:18:00,796
 Goodbye.

305
00:18:08,618 --> 00:18:09,618
 Damn it.

306
00:18:09,643 --> 00:18:11,965
 I'm back to the old man again.

307
00:18:13,464 --> 00:18:15,871
 Mr. Ryo, give up.

308
00:18:15,896 --> 00:18:18,769
 I won't give up.

309
00:18:18,896 --> 00:18:21,896
That old man said he'd
give it to me if I touched it.

310
00:18:21,944 --> 00:18:25,944
I'll be grateful for the
president of 10 billion yen.

311
00:18:36,000 --> 00:18:38,000
 What?

312
00:18:38,000 --> 00:18:41,000
 I can't believe I got there.

313
00:18:41,000 --> 00:18:43,000
 It's not impossible for me.

314
00:18:43,000 --> 00:18:46,000
I don't know if it's the
Maboroshi clan or something,

315
00:18:46,000 --> 00:18:48,000
 but if you can't climb from the inside,

316
00:18:48,000 --> 00:18:50,000
 you have to climb from the outside.

317
00:18:50,000 --> 00:18:52,000
I should have done
this from the beginning.

318
00:18:54,000 --> 00:18:56,000
 Hey, Mr. Ryo.

319
00:18:56,000 --> 00:18:58,000
 Be careful.

320
00:18:59,624 --> 00:19:01,624
 Okay, one more breath.

321
00:19:04,387 --> 00:19:08,041
Thank you for coming all the way here.
I'll give you a compliment.

322
00:19:08,137 --> 00:19:10,000
 You appeared again.

323
00:19:10,000 --> 00:19:11,520
 Good job.

324
00:19:12,000 --> 00:19:14,000
 That's all for the fun.

325
00:19:14,000 --> 00:19:16,000
 I can't give it back like this.

326
00:19:16,000 --> 00:19:19,000
 Oops, I can't take it off.

327
00:19:19,000 --> 00:19:21,000
 Did my body get stiff?

328
00:19:21,000 --> 00:19:23,000
 No, it's fine.

329
00:19:23,000 --> 00:19:24,000
 Hey, wait.

330
00:19:24,000 --> 00:19:26,000
 It's an island house.

331
00:19:27,432 --> 00:19:29,000
 Ouch.

332
00:19:29,000 --> 00:19:32,000
 Ninja art.

333
00:19:32,000 --> 00:19:34,000
 Finish.

334
00:19:40,711 --> 00:19:42,840
 Don't pull it in front of me.

335
00:19:46,000 --> 00:19:47,000
 Damn it.

336
00:19:47,000 --> 00:19:49,000
 That old man.

337
00:19:49,000 --> 00:19:51,000
 He's not an ordinary person.

338
00:19:51,000 --> 00:19:54,000
 Now, are you a snob from Uesugi?

339
00:19:55,468 --> 00:19:57,000
 I did it.

340
00:19:57,000 --> 00:19:59,000
 A golden shachihoko.

341
00:19:59,000 --> 00:20:00,708
 Stop it.

342
00:20:03,000 --> 00:20:06,000
 You can't touch that shachihoko.

343
00:20:06,000 --> 00:20:08,000
 What are you talking about?

344
00:20:08,000 --> 00:20:10,000
You promised to give
it to me if I touched it.

345
00:20:10,000 --> 00:20:12,000
 Anyway, you can't touch it.

346
00:20:12,000 --> 00:20:13,569
 Shut up.

347
00:20:13,594 --> 00:20:16,000
It's not up to you what
to do with my stuff.

348
00:20:16,000 --> 00:20:18,000
 Oh, sorry.

349
00:20:18,000 --> 00:20:19,038
 I said no.

350
00:20:20,975 --> 00:20:22,678
 Let's do it.

351
00:20:22,999 --> 00:20:26,000
 I didn't make it in time.

352
00:20:30,000 --> 00:20:32,000
 It's over.

353
00:20:32,000 --> 00:20:34,000
 I know how you feel.

354
00:20:34,000 --> 00:20:36,000
 I don't need a shachihoko.

355
00:20:36,000 --> 00:20:38,000
 I have a great castle.

356
00:20:38,000 --> 00:20:40,000
 What?

357
00:20:40,000 --> 00:20:42,000
 If you take the shachihoko,

358
00:20:42,000 --> 00:20:44,000
 the castle will be destroyed.

359
00:20:44,000 --> 00:20:46,000
 What?

360
00:20:46,000 --> 00:20:50,810
 I hope no one gets the golden shachihoko.

361
00:20:52,000 --> 00:20:54,000
 What's going on?

362
00:20:58,000 --> 00:21:01,000
 No one can stop this now.

363
00:21:01,000 --> 00:21:05,000
I'll give you the golden
shachihoko as promised.

364
00:21:06,507 --> 00:21:08,507
 What?

365
00:21:24,266 --> 00:21:27,000
Grandpa, it's dangerous.
Let's go.

366
00:21:27,000 --> 00:21:30,000
 I'll take the castle with me.

367
00:21:30,000 --> 00:21:32,000
 Don't talk nonsense.

368
00:21:32,000 --> 00:21:34,000
 You have a good chance.

369
00:21:34,000 --> 00:21:36,000
 Goodbye.

370
00:21:36,000 --> 00:21:38,000
 Hey.

371
00:22:00,647 --> 00:22:04,694
 This is really an illusion.

372
00:22:04,719 --> 00:22:07,233
 No one will believe me.

373
00:22:08,687 --> 00:22:09,687
 What?

374
00:22:09,712 --> 00:22:10,976
 I have this.

375
00:22:16,000 --> 00:22:17,000
 What do you think?

376
00:22:17,000 --> 00:22:19,000
 You were scared, weren't you?

377
00:22:19,000 --> 00:22:22,000
 This is all mine.

378
00:22:22,000 --> 00:22:25,000
 You should keep your eyes on it.

379
00:22:25,000 --> 00:22:27,000
 Especially you.

380
00:22:27,000 --> 00:22:30,000
 You can't live without it.

381
00:22:30,000 --> 00:22:33,000
 I bought it at a souvenir shop.

382
00:22:33,000 --> 00:22:35,000
 It's a fake.

383
00:22:35,000 --> 00:22:37,000
 I don't want it.

384
00:22:37,000 --> 00:22:39,000
 This is what I want.

385
00:22:39,000 --> 00:22:42,000
 Look at this shine.

386
00:22:42,000 --> 00:22:45,000
 Where is this fake?

387
00:22:45,000 --> 00:22:47,000
 It's okay.

388
00:22:47,000 --> 00:22:49,000
 I hit it.

389
00:22:49,000 --> 00:22:50,000
 Oh, no.

390
00:22:50,000 --> 00:22:52,000
 It's gone.

391
00:22:52,000 --> 00:22:54,000
 What's this?

392
00:22:54,000 --> 00:22:57,000
 This is really a fake.

393
00:22:58,000 --> 00:23:01,000
 It's not a good shine.

394
00:23:01,000 --> 00:23:04,000
 It's not a fake either.

395
00:23:04,000 --> 00:23:08,000
 You're the real shachihoko.

396
00:23:19,000 --> 00:23:21,000
 Oh, no.

397
00:23:21,000 --> 00:23:23,000
 I hate this old man.

398
00:23:23,000 --> 00:23:26,000
 I'm not an old man.

399
00:23:26,000 --> 00:23:29,000
 Call me an old man.

400
00:23:29,000 --> 00:23:32,000
 I think an old man is better.

401
00:23:32,000 --> 00:23:34,000
 That's impossible.

402
00:23:34,000 --> 00:23:35,000
 That's right.

403
00:23:35,000 --> 00:23:37,000
 An old man.

404
00:23:37,000 --> 00:23:39,000
 I see.

405
00:23:39,000 --> 00:23:42,000
 Can I keep this?

406
00:23:42,000 --> 00:23:43,000
 Hello.

407
00:23:43,000 --> 00:23:44,000
 Hello.

408
00:23:44,000 --> 00:23:45,000
 Hello.

409
00:23:45,000 --> 00:23:46,000
 Old man.

410
00:23:46,000 --> 00:23:49,000
 The castle is gone.

411
00:23:49,000 --> 00:23:52,000
 It's the best way to have fun.

412
00:23:54,000 --> 00:23:57,000
 Do you want it?

413
00:23:57,000 --> 00:23:59,000
 I want it.

414
00:23:59,000 --> 00:24:01,000
 I want it.

415
00:24:05,000 --> 00:24:07,000
 I'm sorry.

416
00:24:07,000 --> 00:24:11,000
 When you're done cleaning, buy some meat.

417
00:24:11,000 --> 00:24:12,000
 What?

418
00:24:12,000 --> 00:24:15,000
Is it okay to eat something
like that during training?

419
00:24:15,000 --> 00:24:16,000
 It's okay.

420
00:24:16,000 --> 00:24:19,000
 Leave it to me.

421
00:24:19,000 --> 00:24:21,000
 Next time, Ryotsu is training.

422
00:24:21,000 --> 00:24:23,000
 Thank you.

